      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.52,
      "end_seconds": 258.2,
      "duration_seconds": 8.68,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at episodes of supraventricular tachycardia or atrial fibrillation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.3,
      "end_seconds": 262.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.36,
      "end_seconds": 289.77,
      "duration_seconds": 26.41,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now episodes of supraventricular tachycardia is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let's book an ECG to look into palpitations. Try blowing hard against a closed mouth and nose when it starts. I'm going to send a referral to the cardiology clinic. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.57,
      "end_seconds": 296.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "yes, um, I'll bear that in mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.97,
      "end_seconds": 301.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "I'd like to to see you again after the monitor"
    },
